WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.866 --> 00:00:04.931
(jazzy rhythmic music)

00:00:04.931 --> 00:00:06.393
- [Voiceover] Yo, Chris.

00:00:06.393 --> 00:00:07.531
- [Chris] Hey man, what's up?

00:00:07.531 --> 00:00:08.529
- Not much, not much.

00:00:08.529 --> 00:00:09.412
How was your weekend?

00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:11.409
- [Chris] Um, I know
you don't really care.

00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:13.539
You're just asking so I
ask you about your weekend.

00:00:13.539 --> 00:00:15.054
Everybody knows you
went snowboarding, bro.

00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:16.122
It's all over Instagram.

00:00:16.122 --> 00:00:17.287
Go easy on the hashtags.

00:00:17.287 --> 00:00:17.960
What about you?

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.680
How was yours?

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.212
- Oh, you know, it was cool, man.

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:22.697
Snowboarding up in Mammoth, fresh pow pow.

00:00:22.697 --> 00:00:23.649
It was dope.

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:25.228
Here, check it out.

00:00:25.228 --> 00:00:26.570
- You guys talking about the weekend?

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.661
Mammoth sounds fun.

00:00:27.661 --> 00:00:29.194
Actually went to Disney
on Ice on Saturday.

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:31.191
- [Chris] This guy, he
always tries to relate to you

00:00:31.191 --> 00:00:32.904
and be your friend, but
at the end of the day

00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:34.112
he's still got a job to do.

00:00:34.112 --> 00:00:35.598
- Anyway, I need 20
copies of this from you,

00:00:35.598 --> 00:00:37.223
stapled and collated for
the meeting later, okay?

00:00:37.223 --> 00:00:38.209
- [Chris] Sure.

00:00:38.209 --> 00:00:41.738
(jazzy rhythmic music)

00:00:41.738 --> 00:00:43.410
- [Chris] Alright, coffee.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.685
- [Voiceover] Chris!

00:00:45.685 --> 00:00:47.264
- [Chris] Hey...

00:00:47.264 --> 00:00:48.750
What the hell is your name?

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.608
I wanna say it starts with a J.

00:00:50.608 --> 00:00:52.883
Josh? Jamie?

00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:54.083
I actually have to go make copies

00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:55.380
for Shane's meeting later, so.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.538
- Ah, stapled and collated (laughs)?

00:00:58.538 --> 00:01:00.047
- [Chris] Shyeah, pretty much.

00:01:00.047 --> 00:01:03.901
Okay, have a good one, dude.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.434
- [No Name Guy] Peace bro!

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:08.267
- [Chris] I shoulda really
remembered his name.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.871
(jazzy rhythmic music)

00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:15.862
Crap, did she see me staring?

00:01:15.862 --> 00:01:17.186
- [Woman] Hey, making copies?

00:01:17.186 --> 00:01:19.461
- [Chris] Oh, yeah (laughs).

00:01:19.461 --> 00:01:20.529
- You seem so tired.

00:01:20.529 --> 00:01:23.084
- [Chris] Yeah, I'm
gonna get some coffee--

00:01:23.084 --> 00:01:25.382
- You think you're tired, I'm exhausted.

00:01:25.382 --> 00:01:27.356
I've been planning Dan's party all week.

00:01:27.356 --> 00:01:29.026
- [Chris] Here he is, the planner.

00:01:29.026 --> 00:01:31.554
Constantly inviting you and
your coworkers out for drinks,

00:01:31.554 --> 00:01:34.248
food, a movie, but whatever
it is, you always come up

00:01:34.248 --> 00:01:35.595
with an excuse.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.474
Ah, see ya guys.

00:01:38.474 --> 00:01:42.299
(jazzy rhythmic music)

00:01:47.785 --> 00:01:48.806
- [Woman] What are you thinking about?

00:01:48.806 --> 00:01:50.455
- Uh, I don't know.

00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:52.066
I'm just glad I have
someone to talk to, I guess.

00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:54.945
- Yeah, same.

00:01:56.975 --> 00:01:57.807
- What?

00:01:57.807 --> 00:02:00.146
- [Woman] Nothing.

